<p>Russia and Ukraine accused each other on Sunday of violating a U.S.-brokered three-day ceasefire announced by President Trump, as both sides reported drone, artillery and battlefield attacks during the pause. The truce was part of a U.S.-led diplomatic effort that, after months of shuttle diplomacy, has not ended the war. Ukrainian officials said Russian drone strikes near the front line killed three people and that more than 200 battlefield clashes had occurred since early Saturday. Russia’s Defence Ministry accused Ukraine of breaching the ceasefire, said it had downed 57 Ukrainian drones over the previous day and said Russian forces “responded in kind” on the battlefield. RT, citing the Russian Defence Ministry, said Moscow had recorded 16,071 Ukrainian ceasefire violations since Friday.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/PL9ct7qzjpYB0RoYogYKmlGiJ4AdL0lhz0kegNLOvzmVu3pnytuzhbJYDhagJVKxw-ZZgbG58xlbpZx5lrv-tO6EntkNXNSyhXYeArPgs7h4bFv-n64mL9KZvwfJ8VJy5GwpBpFQsaq3rh1e4k0BGrhtcfWK6aOUVU7kdy3q7C1nmrn6Fp1s65vsxxsqx-do4eMpXB47DmjdV7jyM7BGbj-WGQDKUUcamU8-mB7Mv1mW7Xv5eWJcwYCKIe2Mge48qsHVBuccig' alt='Ukrainian ground forces ride in vehicles along a road covered with a net to protect vehicles from drone attacks at an undisclosed location in Ukraine.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reduced barrage: Kyiv’s air force said Russia launched 27 long-range drones overnight, fewer than usual, and that Ukrainian air defences intercepted them.</li><li>Civilian injuries: Local officials in Kharkiv, Kherson and Dnipropetrovsk reported 16 wounded, including four children, and damage to infrastructure.</li><li>Russian claims: Russian officials said Ukrainian attacks targeted civilian sites in Crimea, Krasnodar, Belgorod, Kursk, Kaluga and Rostov, and Belgorod Governor Vyacheslav Gladkov said five civilians, including a teenager, were injured.</li><li>Exchange plan: The ceasefire arrangement also included a proposed swap of 1,000 prisoners of war from each side, but the timing remained unclear.</li></ul><blockquote>On the frontline, the Russian army is not complying with the ceasefire and is not even really trying to. - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian presidency: Zelenskyy said Ukraine would retaliate for any aggression shown by Moscow during the pause. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3353070/ukraine-reports-multiple-casualties-despite-trump-backed-truce-russia'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Russian Defence Ministry: The ministry said its running tally included 676 strikes on Russian positions, 6,331 drone attacks and eight attempted assaults by Ukrainian forces. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639847-ukraine-victory-day-ceasefire-violations/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Kremlin: Spokesman Dmitry Peskov said reaching a peace agreement on Ukraine would take a long time and involve complicated details. (<a href='https://www.iltempo.it/esteri/2026/05/10/news/ucraina-zelensky-accusa-la-russia-ha-violato-tregua-e-mosca-hanno-attaccato-loro--47664415/'>Il Tempo</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3353070/ukraine-reports-multiple-casualties-despite-trump-backed-truce-russia'>Ukraine and Russia accuse each other of breaking US-brokered ceasefire</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-and-russia-accuse-each-other-of-breaching-us-backed-ceasefire'>Ukraine and Russia accuse each other of breaching US-backed ceasefire</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/russia-accuses-ukraine-violating-us-brokered-day-truce-132823137'>Russia accuses Ukraine of violating U.S.-brokered three-day truce</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639847-ukraine-victory-day-ceasefire-violations/'>Ukraine violated Victory Day ceasefire over 16,000 times – Russian MOD</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/new